        "original_id": "73b6acd9-4362-5c7b-9eef-ea4cb1b4043c",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: John Flammang Schrank, Theodore Roosevelt\n- Places: New York, Milwaukee, Wisconsin, United States\n- Roles: U.S. President, 26th President of the United States\n- Events: Attempted assassination of Theodore Roosevelt, Progressive Era\n- Topics: American politics\n\nFacts:\n- Theodore Roosevelt Jr. was born on October 27, 1858, and he later served as the 26th President of the United States from 1901 to 1909.\n- Theodore Roosevelt was an American statesman, author, explorer, soldier, naturalist, and reformer.\n- Theodore Roosevelt was a leader of the Republican Party and a driving force for the Progressive Era in the United States in the early 20th century.\n- John Flammang Schrank was born on March 5, 1876, and was a resident of New York.\n- On October 14, 1912, John Flammang Schrank attempted to assassinate former U.S. President Theodore Roosevelt in Milwaukee, Wisconsin.\n- John Flammang Schrank died on September 15, 1943, and Theodore Roosevelt died on January 6, 1919.",
